{"title":"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems\">2019 AMC 10B #6</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems\">2019 AMC 12B #4</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Simpler_Solution_1,_No_Experimentation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Simpler Solution 1, No Experimentation)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Comprehensive🧠)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Comprehensive🧠)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There is a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/d/98dc20d6f1386364161a4508d2ff25986eed1fd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)! + (n+2)! = n! \\cdot 440$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"225\" height=\"18\" />. What is the sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/3/0d346d6b6bffb3d088857498848276d580c012e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }3\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }8\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }10\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }11\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"380\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/4/e94a76dd637eee784abfc844bcc187bc69d72464.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{split}&amp; (n+1)n! + (n+2)(n+1)n! = 440 \\cdot n! \\\\ \\Rightarrow \\ &amp;n![n+1 + (n+2)(n+1)] = 440 \\cdot n! \\\\ \\Rightarrow \\ &amp;n + 1 + n^2 + 3n + 2 = 440 \\\\ \\Rightarrow \\ &amp;n^2 + 4n - 437 = 0\\end{split}\\]\" width=\"325\" height=\"95\" />\n</p><p>Solving by the quadratic formula, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/2/a023ee925fa8d3fd93a37f46364df404ee8d89d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\frac{-4\\pm \\sqrt{16+437\\cdot4}}{2} = \\frac{-4\\pm 42}{2} = \\frac{38}{2} = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"372\" height=\"42\" /> (since clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/1/821d5b948fd2e8a82be18042d192710914b5e819.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />). The answer is therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/0/cc0bfc50fc2473f35c63580ea31e43dd3aa38806.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 9 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"129\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Dividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/a/95acebc265a9f6c6779a1c3e16f867517e875b6a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(n+1)+(n+2)(n+1)=440 \\Rightarrow n^2+4n-437=0 \\Rightarrow (n-19)(n+23)=0.\\]\" width=\"544\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Instead of prime factorizing 437, which could take some time, we can notice that the two factors of 437 we need (if they exist) need to be pretty close - their difference is 4. Then, we can try a few numbers close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/e/77e20ed59fa013138bee79301b0dd31534880a23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{400} = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />, so we find 19 and 23 as factors.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is non-negative, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1ba21440957dd537f17834562b567ea84248f4c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=19$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/0/cc0bfc50fc2473f35c63580ea31e43dd3aa38806.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 9 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"129\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Dividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> as before gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/2/a42d89bee1ecf65da91202c91ee88012635736cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)+(n+1)(n+2)=440$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"245\" height=\"20\" />. Now factor out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/c/99cb3f3a8b3bbfc702c5863d16602a06cded535d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/d/ded98c42b6ff670c17e4156389c227f01a4c5942.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)(n+3)=440$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"163\" height=\"18\" />. By considering the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/b/b7bac8d158ad07b42ad9889011a7e4e67851a82d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$440$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, a bit of experimentation gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/f/e6f46a9e0ab409c6c256eec4b5016ec9ca874cfe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1=20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/4/6344e40f77ba5178ab64e65c57ad7b5c153262e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+3=22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1ba21440957dd537f17834562b567ea84248f4c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=19$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/0/cc0bfc50fc2473f35c63580ea31e43dd3aa38806.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 9 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"129\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/1632e151890c4d4661838e345bb94afd164db4bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)! + (n+2)! = (n+1)n! + (n+2)(n+1)n! = 440 \\cdot n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"475\" height=\"20\" />, the result can be factored into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/0/f7066b873664571ed8d9ba5112824cdb5e922750.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)(n+3)n!=440 \\cdot n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"211\" height=\"20\" /> and divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> on both sides to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/d/ded98c42b6ff670c17e4156389c227f01a4c5942.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)(n+3)=440$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"163\" height=\"18\" />. From there, it is easier to complete the square with the quadratic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/3/ea3e70c62aaab0dca2d6b289775e76c8bc2e9456.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)(n+3) = n^2 + 4n + 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"231\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/f/6afca704f98098fd57ce728de78ff178ffd18cc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2+4n+4=441 \\Rightarrow (n+2)^2=441$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"289\" height=\"21\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/7/b8764197f5186bd985a80b8a20831f9fc7bcd100.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=19,-23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"17\" />, and since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/4/0247db3d702b5ce6be98f50771750a2723cddcea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1ba21440957dd537f17834562b567ea84248f4c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=19$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> and the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/0/cc0bfc50fc2473f35c63580ea31e43dd3aa38806.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 9 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"129\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~Randomlygenerated\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/0/66069cde13f52c05f55e9fd9f6800234e5b1395c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)! + (n+2)! = 440 \\cdot n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"227\" height=\"20\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/f/53ffe565e3cda7d1d91484034b9ff844623d9c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)n! + (n+2)(n+1)n! = 440 \\cdot n!.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"311\" height=\"20\" /> Factoring out the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/5/3158908ccc7ad52781e8beb9a5ac5aba03b0a640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!(n + 1 + (n+1)(n+2)) = 440 \\cdot n!.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"295\" height=\"20\" /> Expand this to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/e/5fe47928f33609c4a7b640ebc8bf6e8aa281f23b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!(n^2 + 4n + 3) = 440 \\cdot n!.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"209\" height=\"21\" /> Factor this and divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/9/4f9f17168605b8b64d32902c914598efc84e1b29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n + 1)(n + 3) = 440.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"171\" height=\"20\" /> If we take the prime factorization of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/b/b7bac8d158ad07b42ad9889011a7e4e67851a82d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$440$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> we see that it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/d/90dd29d92ab3d3c7ca7144a0edc100b7baf7f9ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^3 * 5 * 11.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"17\" /> Intuitively, we can find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/6/606e393c8e92a0a1769a15a6cac5e91426b0d528.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 1 = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/0/c605f3d3a24c35950c348857b7e5d9a16ca9a0f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 3 = 22.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" /> Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/a/c5a43ed1f0530f16bbbc786ba1f9e8fd14fbffd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 19.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> Since the problem asks for the sum of the didgits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, we finally calculate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/3/6639552b29a3b33bcd048300a8dde74e0e84590f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 9 = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> and get answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/a/95a37e2c613248cd21b3266be23fe9b0b6e1ac11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~pnacham\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Factor out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> from the left side of the equation:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/6/246c8369b9f36a0153d4e0106fe8b3159bf6f0f7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(n+1)! + (n+2)! = (n+1)n! + (n+2)(n+1)n!\\]\" width=\"389\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/d/64d052651cac743126e633fae40baf07c88c7232.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= (n+1)n! \\left[ 1 + (n+2) \\right]\\]\" width=\"189\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/3/ed3750b1065712b7325d20ba322c208e0d63b10c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= (n+1)(n+3) \\cdot n!\\]\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Setting this equal to the given expression <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/d/dbd93b27b45bbb30125e1fae7d5555edfa08c4a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$440 \\cdot n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/d/23de0ea28e44ed5ee29e77ce37152df34185da68.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(n+3)(n+1) \\cdot n! = 440 \\cdot n!\\]\" width=\"219\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Dividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f344e7d8b14a7886fc7fb72da53cd0a3271dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be02fa41435cf2dbae55bd5dee5a04a468ded9fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(n+3)(n+1) = 440\\]\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>To solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/d/83dd037e686ffc7373e9ea3249008959b4416a7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = n+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"15\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/f/79f2dfeb731d99efe555bc2d8746d1af3f3812c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+3) = a+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"123\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/8/ce8bd1984059ed564936478200607b398eb02f13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1) = a-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"123\" height=\"20\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/f/f5f6c7bf8dd98b3fb0e84959e6a5aa61c1600ea5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a+1)(a-1) = 440\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f3492b40e8443c99c6a7a6e206a0927cfb129b2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2 - 1 = 440\\]\" width=\"98\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/6/796e24b6524bf07b1c3d3b20232eef28b706c9b7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a^2 = 441\\]\" width=\"67\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/1/151c59b7036e94592711d424fe7e7613c0152636.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a = 21\\]\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Substituting back for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/a/73aad48381823618da850b0e5af825cd20ebc3fb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n+2 = 21 \\implies n = 19\\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>The sum of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/2/702559b246d9e4c8727b15a72dccc4052a00384d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 9 = \\boxed{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"96\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Ipimath\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Simpler_Solution_1.2C_No_Experimentation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Simpler_Solution_1,_No_Experimentation)\">Solution 7 (Simpler Solution 1, No Experimentation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Simpler Solution 1, No Experimentation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Like in solution 1, continue until <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/b/d7b5b0f7c17687b02412bc2562201cee3d7e4c8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2 + 4n - 437 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Quadratic formula:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/8/6c889f7a1abdc15b11b19c0894ab0bad8b53564e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{-4 \\pm \\sqrt{1764}}{2}\\]\" width=\"97\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, assume 1764 is a perfect square. The last digit of 1764 is 4, meaning that the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/7/7f79d5405bbc93e5f2b97e47d94ac60251e8ceda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2 = 1764$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> ends in either 2 or 8. Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/c/64c2a93af681cbc914d2c860343175b02d1adf72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{16} &lt; \\sqrt{17} &lt; \\sqrt{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"150\" height=\"21\" />, so taking the former of the two, we have that our possible square roots are 42 or 48. It then follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/b/c7b231d67a4e73909f525435587b81644427f951.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40^2 &lt; k^2 &lt; 50^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/5/0e5c83cc0c639fc2ed843bbe2d3d209fb478b104.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> is much closer to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/1/6212ca78555150d1747270c7f186c1cae3bae46a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/a/46a6d5052d1de3dbed09284a27ab36f429a43655.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50^2$\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />, so our desired <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/d/4cdf80e56000a5493c26a0119d5784982d78fc68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/e/8aeed81ffe5071b2d5d291bca220b3480da708cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> and the sum of the digits is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/7/cd7ae6c302dec5c5be789f3d4d9be37d000d0772.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p><p>To learn this mental math trick, the video below credited to the Organic Chemistry Tutor quite well verses this topic.\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=44lpu2IFZvQ\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=44lpu2IFZvQ</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/7p_ESPPF2es\">https://youtu.be/7p_ESPPF2es</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ba6w1OhXqOQ?t=1956\">https://youtu.be/ba6w1OhXqOQ?t=1956</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/7xf_g3YQk00\">https://youtu.be/7xf_g3YQk00</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_4\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/6YFN_hwotUk\">https://youtu.be/6YFN_hwotUk</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.28Comprehensive.F0.9F.A7.A0.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(Comprehensive🧠)\">Video Solution(Comprehensive🧠)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(Comprehensive🧠)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gZOghSqS18o\">https://youtu.be/gZOghSqS18o</a>\n</p><p>~Ani_lytical\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B\">2019 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a